Package: nidooffice-desktop
Version: 0.13.1
Section: editors
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: ca-certificates, curl, desktop-file-utils, libccid, libcairo2, libdrm2, libgbm1, libnss3, libnss3-tools, libpango-1.0-0, libxcomposite1, libxdamage1, libxfixes3, libxkbcommon0, libxrandr2, libatk1.0-0t64 | libatk1.0-0, libatk-bridge2.0-0t64 | libatk-bridge2.0-0, libcups2t64 | libcups2, libasound2t64 | libasound2, libgtk-3-0t64 | libgtk-3-0, opensc, opensc-pkcs11, pcscd, python3, squashfs-tools
Recommends: nidooffice-cli (>= 0.2.0)
Maintainer: Nido Holdings <support@nido-holdings.com>
Homepage: https://office.nido-holdings.com
Description: NidoOffice Desktop AI Office Suite installer for Ubuntu-Nido
 Resolves and downloads the latest official NidoOffice Desktop AppImage runtime
 from GitHub Releases (with SHA256 verification) into /opt/NidoOffice, configures
 GNOME Wayland IME launch integration, sets AppArmor userns policy, and registers
 desktop & Office MIME defaults.
